From 2b2af79cc88e01eed74e59ba435d870317adcbb8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shammah Chancellor <shammah.chancellor@notvalid.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 06:25:18 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] chronik: native indexer, Service and WebSocket handler

Port chronik-indexer/src/indexer.rs (open with schema checks, resync
against the host tip incl. behind/ahead/forked and shutdown, block
connect/disconnect/finalize/invalidate, mempool events, tx finality,
TxNumCache, avalanche and merkle caching, LOKAD/scripthash reindex,
perf stats) and chronik-http ws.rs (subscription parsing, per-session
limits, biased message order, proto WsMsg building).

Locking follows the design: the writer builds its write transaction
without the state lock, commits and updates the mempool under the
exclusive lock, and publishes to subscribers after releasing it; Host is
never called under the exclusive lock. Queries take a snapshot (shared
lock plus one read transaction), exposed by indexer_impl.h for the
query handlers. Event failures put the indexer in a failed state and
throw to the host adapter, which aborts like Node::ok_or_abort.

Token indexing plugs in through a narrow TokenIndex seam
(token_index.h), implemented by the eCash token index; enabling it
without an implementation fails closed instead of wiping the index.

Service (service.h) ties together indexer, router, query pool, the
-chronikbind Beast listeners, pause/resume and the subscription hub,
and offers the in-process HTTP/WS entry points for host servers.

Tests: 52 cases, including the design's connect/disconnect property
(dump equality over random chains with spends and reorgs up to depth
6, with and without LOKAD, scripthash and token indexes), resync cases,
a FakeHost, WS handler and Service tests (real TCP listener, interrupt
answering 503). Rust's test_plugin_versions is not ported (no plugins).

Tier: eCash

Coordinator integration provenance (metrics369):
Introduce service observer plumbing and WS connection lifecycle at first consumers. Successful guarded writer commits update indexed height with no extra per-block lock, ignored failed-indexer events do not advance it. Initial snapshot is startup-only; observer exceptions never alter protocol/indexer success. Three deferred native observer controls included across their owners.
All build/runtime/observer controls deferred by user compile-first policy; ordered source replay is not runtime approval.
